EXT. STRANDED GONDOLA - ALPINE SLOPE - DUSK

A red cable car dangles two hundred feet above a snowfield, swaying slightly. The lights of the valley are a long way below. Wind sighs in the cables.

INT. GONDOLA - CONTINUOUS

Six people share a steel cabin built for eight. Windows fog with breath. A flask passes hand to hand.

MIREILLE CASTANEDA, 60s, in a white wool coat, sits in the corner with her eyes closed, rubbing a rosary between her thumb and finger. OZZIE BERGSTROM, 30s, a lanky snowboarder, leans against the door, thumbing a dead phone. NKECHI OBI, 40s, a nurse, tends to DARIUSZ PAWLAK, 70s, whose hand trembles around a thermos. XIMENA TORRES, 20s, squeezes onto the bench beside them, scrolling through a map with no signal. And CORNELIUS "NEIL" ATWOOD, 50s, stands at the window and watches the dark.

He turns from the window. She glances at him. They both look away.

Ozzie slides to the floor. Ximena shifts to make room for his legs, and Nkechi tucks a blanket around Dariusz's knees. Mireille sighs.

NEIL
How long has it been?

NKECHI
Forty minutes.

NEIL
It feels like four hours.

OZZIE
It always does.

XIMENA
Has anyone tried the emergency cord?

DARIUSZ
It's been pulled twice.

NKECHI
Both times, a recorded voice said help was coming.

MIREILLE
(eyes closed)
Help is always coming.

Silence. The cabin sways. Everyone shifts their weight at once, and Ozzie curses. They steady. Nkechi glances at Dariusz, who has gone pale.

NKECHI (CONT'D)
Drink some water.

DARIUSZ
I am fine.

NKECHI
I know. Drink.

He does. She smiles and pats his hand. Neil returns to the window. Ximena folds up her phone. Ozzie tilts his head back against the door.

The cabin lurches once and then, with a long, heavy groan, begins to move.
